-- title:
--   Moment recurrence bound for histogram recursions
-- statement:
--   Let $h$ be a finite list of pairs $(w, c)$ (child width $w$ with multiplicity $c$) with $0 < w < m$, $m \ge 2$, $W > 0$, $0 < \tau \le 1$, and suppose the moment condition $\mu_\tau(h; m) < W$ (`histMoment h m τ < W`). If $c : \mathbb N \to \mathbb R$ is monotone and satisfies, for all $f \ge 1$,
--
--   $$c(mf) \le \frac{1}{W}\sum_{(w,c_w) \in h} c_w\, c(wf) + K,$$
--
--   then there is $A$ with $c(x) \le A\, x^{\tau}$ for all $x \ge 1$.
--
--   This is the cost recurrence of a recursive interchange network whose children are described by the histogram $h$.
--
--   In Lean:
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem R6.MomentRec.moment_recurrence_bound (h : List (ℕ × ℕ)) (m W : ℕ) (τ K : ℝ) (c : ℕ → ℝ)
--       (hm : 2 ≤ m) (hτ0 : 0 < τ) (hτ1 : τ ≤ 1)
--       (hw : ∀ p ∈ h, 0 < p.1 ∧ p.1 < m) (hW : 0 < W)
--       (hmom : histMoment h m τ < W) (hmono : Monotone c)
--       (hrec : ∀ f : ℕ, 1 ≤ f →
--         c (m * f) ≤ (h.map fun p => (p.2 : ℝ) * c (p.1 * f)).sum / W + K) :
--       ∃ A : ℝ, ∀ x : ℕ, 1 ≤ x → c x ≤ A * (x : ℝ) ^ τ
--   ```
